 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to hotel and motel taxes in Ulster\ncounty",
    "basePrintNo": "S6896",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6896-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1202-l, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6896\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to hotel and motel taxes in\nUlster county\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation authorizes Ulster County to impose by local law, a tax\non hotel and motel occupancy of up to four percent of the charge.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Tax Law by amending section 1202-I which authorizes\nthe imposition of a hotel and motel occupancy tax in Ulster County. The\nrate of the tax shall not exceed 4% of the per diem (daily) rental rate\nfor each room. The tax shall also apply to \"bed and breakfast\" and\n\"tourist\" and 'short-term renter facilities.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date which shall be immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would allow Ulster County to impose a hotel and motel\ntax. The rate of such tax shall not exceed 4% of the per diem (daily)\nrental rate for each room. The tax shall also apply to \"bed and break-\nfast\" and 'tourist\" facilities such as Airbrib. Pursuant to the Munici-\npal Home Rule Law, acounty may adopt local laws that relate to the levy\nand administration of local taxes if authorized by the State legisla-\nture. Ulster County has requested special legislation which will enable\nthem to collect a hotel and motel tax in an effort to raise additional\nrevenue for the county.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the state. The county will collect additional revenues which\nwill be used to reduce the burden on local taxpayers.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
